kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[1]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,tui52,"multi-round-turn-not-truncated","The TUI MUST drain the agent XyEvent stream for a user prompt until the stream ends (returns None) and MUST NOT stop at the first XyEvent::TurnEnd. The react loop emits one TurnEnd per ReAct iteration; a tool-calling turn spans multiple iterations (the model calls a tool then continues in a later iteration) so intermediate TurnEnds are single-iteration boundaries not the end of the whole user turn. The turn-fully-done signal (when to clear the mutable tail and reset streaming state) MUST be stream termination (None) delivered as an explicit end-of-stream message to the main loop, NOT a mid-stream TurnEnd. Evidence: spawn_drain broke on the first TurnEnd so tool-calling turns had their continuation events dropped and the REPL appeared to hang after a tool call; print mode consumes the whole stream via while-let-Some and is unaffected, confirming the multi-TurnEnd protocol is by design and the bug is TUI-side.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[3]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui52,"tool-turn-continuation-reaches-tui","a turn runs a tool call then the model produces a final text reply across multiple ReAct iterations","the XyEvent stream is drained by the TUI and rendered","the final text reply after the tool call is rendered in the TUI (not dropped) and the mutable tail reflects the continuation"
  tui52,"drain-breaks-on-stream-end","the TUI drain task is inspected","the stream consumption loop is read","the loop breaks on stream None or external cancellation and does NOT break on an intermediate TurnEnd"
  tui52,"tail-cleared-on-stream-end","a multi-iteration tool-calling turn finishes","the stream returns None","the mutable tail is cleared and streaming state is reset exactly once when the stream ends (not on the intermediate TurnEnd that precedes the continuation round)"
